.TH CSTRING_PREPEND 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cstring_prepend \- prepend a C string to the beginning
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cstring.h>

ccol_retval_t cstring_prepend(cstr s, const char *str);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
This function inserts the null-terminated C string str in front of all
the characters of s, moving the existing content right to make room.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
s     String to change
str   C string to prepend (must not be NULL)
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success              - The prepend succeeded
ccol_invalid_args         - str is NULL
ccol_container_full       - The result would overflow a size_t
ccol_not_enough_memory    - The reallocation failed
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Asserts if s is NULL
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cstring_append (3),
.BR cstring_insert (3)
